  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No prior evidence exists, so the first experiment should establish the simplest, most interpretable baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the minimal RNA configuration with a standard, well-understood encoder (PCA to 2000 dims) and no aggregation or fusion complexity. This tests whether a basic single-modality RNA model provides a meaningful accuracy floor. Establishing this baseline first is critical because: (1) it tells us whether RNA signal alone is sufficient or whether we must invest remaining budget in image/multimodal directions; (2) it provides a reference accuracy against which every more complex configuration (multiprofile, learned encoders, multimodal fusion) can be judged for marginal benefit; (3) it changes the fewest design choices, so any future performance difference can be attributed to a specific axis rather than confounded by multiple simultaneous changes. With 9 experiments remaining, this single clean baseline maximizes the information gained per experiment and guides the next logical step (e.g., adding image modality or upgrading the encoder)."
}

